            {
              "id": "dfc47eb0-ea9d-4666-bbad-914bda5a5e59",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>The Routledge Companion to Video Game Studies</strong></em> is a collection of essays edited by Mark J.P. Wold &amp; Bernard Perron, published by Routledge, April 13, 2016."
            },
            {
              "id": "6a1aa24f-7ae2-49cf-be04-04fe3a2a07ab",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "a7ba3397-a326-4b1f-86bc-db5030c93f81",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>The number of publications dealing with video game studies has exploded over the course of the last decade, but the field has produced few comprehensive reference works. </em>The Routledge Companion to Video Game Studies<em>, compiled by well-known video game scholars Mark J. P. Wolf and Bernard Perron, aims to address the ongoing theoretical and methodological development of game studies, providing students, scholars, and game designers with a definitive look at contemporary video game studies.<br><br>Features include:</em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "d1899c5f-6368-4ad7-a739-c2d24d985cd6",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            }
          ]
